  "bug": {
    "bug_id": "Compress-37",
    "project": "Compress",
    "summary": "Parsing PAX headers fails with NegativeArraySizeException",
    "description": "The \nTarArchiveInputStream.parsePaxHeaders\nmethod fails with a \nNegativeArraySizeException\nwhen there is an empty line at the end of the headers.\n\nThe inner loop starts reading the length, but it gets a newline (10) and ends up subtracting '0' (48) from it; the result is a negative length that blows up an attempt to allocate the \nrest\narray.\n\nI would say that a check to see if \nch\nis less the '0' and break the loop if it is.\n\nI used \nnpm pack aws-sdk@2.2.16\nto generate a tarball with this issue."
  },
